&Q000741 = A hymn to Šul-pa-e (Šul-pa-e A)
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.4.31.1
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.4.31.1&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

@div version 1 (Version A)

1.1. ur-saŋ %e uru₂-bad₃-da %s iti₇-gin₇! e₃-a
#lem: ursaŋ[warrior]; urubad[city]; itud[moon]; e[leave]
#tr.en: Hero, who shines forth like moonlight over the upper city! 
#etcsl: line-id=1.1

1.2. ur-saŋ {d}šul-pa-e₃ iri-bad₃-da <iti₇-gin₇ e₃-a>
#lem: ursaŋ[warrior]; Šulpae[1]DN; iribad[the upper part of a city]; itud[moon]; e[leave]
#tr.en: Hero @wDN{Šul-pa-e}, who shines forth like moonlight over the upper city! 
#etcsl: line-id=1.2

1.3. alim-ma mu tuku {d}šul-pa-e₃ %e uru₂-bad₃-da %s <iti₇-gin₇ e₃-a>
#lem: alim[bison]; mu[name]; tuku[acquire]; Šulpae[1]DN; urubad[city]; itud[moon]; e[leave]
#tr.en: Eminent and famous @wDN{Šul-pa-e}, who shines forth like moonlight over the upper city! 
#etcsl: line-id=1.3

1.4. lugal me gal-gal diŋir pa e₃-a
#lem: lugal[king]; me[Being]; gal[big]; diŋir[deity]; pa[branch]; e[leave]
#tr.en: Lord of great divine powers, god who appears in glory, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.4

1.5. {d}šul-pa-e₃ me gal-gal diŋir pa e₃-a
#lem: Šulpae[1]DN; me[Being]; gal[big]; diŋir[deity]; pa[branch]; e[leave]
#tr.en: @wDN{Šul-pa-e}, of great divine powers, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.5

1.6. nir-ŋal₂ me₃-a u₂-šim kalam-ma sud-sud
#lem: nirŋal[authoritative]; me[battle]; ušim[greenery]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; sud[distant]
#tr.en: god who appears in glory, lordly in battle, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.6

1.7. en a₂ mah il₂-il₂-i ŋiš gaz gu₂-erim₂ ra
#lem: en[lord]; a[arm]; mah[great]; il[raise]; ŋeš[wood]; gaz[kill]; guʾerim[hostile]; rah[beat]
#tr.en: who makes vegetation grow tall in the Land! Lord who raises his great arms, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.7

1.8. mu-us₂-a gu₂-tuku a-a {d}en-lil₂-la₂
#lem: us[accompany]; gutuku[perfect]; aya[father]; Enlil[1]DN
#tr.en: battle-club that smashes all enemies! Pre-eminent brother-in-law of Father @wDN{Enlil}, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.8

1.9. šul zid {d}en-lil₂-la₂ mu mah-zu mu-un-pad₃
#lem: šul[youth]; zid[right]; Enlil[1]DN; mu[name]; mah[great]; pad[find]
#tr.en: good youth! @wDN{Enlil} has named your august name. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.9

1.10. nir-ŋal₂ {ŋiš}tukul-a lipiš me₃-a
#lem: nirŋal[authoritative]; tukul[weapon]; lipiš[inner body]; me[battle]
#tr.en: Lordly with weapons in the thick of battle! Owner of the rebel lands, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.10

1.11. lu₂ ki-bal-a-ke₄ nir-ŋal₂ ki-bal-a
#lem: lu[person]; kibala[rebel land]; nirŋal[authoritative]; kibala[rebel land]
#tr.en: lordly in the rebel lands, my king, you are an august god! 
#etcsl: line-id=1.11

1.12. lugal-ŋu₁₀ za-e %e dim₃-me-er %s mah-me-en
#lem: lugal[king]; zaʾe[you]; dimmer[deity]N; mah[great]
#tr.en: You are an august god, and your wife is an august queen. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.12

1.13. za-e %e dim₃-me-er %s mah-me-en dam-zu %e ga!-ša!-an! %s mah-me-en
#lem: zaʾe[you]; dimmer[deity]N; mah[great]; dam[spouse]; gašan[lady]N; mah[great]
#tr.en: You are beloved by @wDN{Ninḫursaŋa}. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.13

#etcsl#text Text U₃-MU-UN for ga-ša-an

1.14. {d}nin-hur#-saŋ-ŋa₂-ke₄ ki aŋ₂-ŋa₂-ni za-e-me-en
#lem: Ninhursaŋak[1]DN; ki[place]; aŋ[measure]; zaʾe[you]
#tr.en: You are a hero before whom the gods are very fearful. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.14

1.15. ur-saŋ# ni₂ gal diŋir-re-e-ne-me-en
#lem: ursaŋ[warrior]; ni[fear]; gal[big]; diŋir[deity]
#tr.en: Hero @wDN{Šul-pa-e}, lordly in heaven and on earth, my ……, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.15

1.16. ur-saŋ# {d}šul-pa-e₃-a an ki-a nir-ŋal₂
#lem: ursaŋ[warrior]; Šulpae[1]DN; an[sky]; ki[place]; nirŋal[authoritative]
#tr.en: may your name be truly called upon in all the foreign lands! 
#etcsl: line-id=1.16

1.17. [...] X-ŋu₁₀ mu-zu kur-kur-ra zid-de₃-eš he₂-pad₃-de₃
#lem: X; X; mu[name]; kur[mountain(s)]; zid[right]; pad[find]
#tr.en: My king, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.17

1.18. lugal#-ŋu₁₀ nam-mah-zu kur-kur-ra zid-de₃-eš he₂-pad₃-de₃
#lem: lugal[king]; nammah[greatness]; kur[mountain(s)]; zid[right]; pad[find]
#tr.en: may your greatness be truly called upon in all the foreign lands! 
#etcsl: line-id=1.18

1.19. [...] X mah-a a-ŋi₆ zig₃-ga u₁₈-lu lu₂-ra te-a
#lem: X; X; mah[great]; aŋi[wave]; zig[rise]; ulu[south wind]; lu[person]; teŋ[approach]
#tr.en: August ……, rising flood, storm which approaches mankind! 
#etcsl: line-id=1.19

1.20. [nam]-lu₂#-ulu₃ mušen ni₂ te-a-gin₇ šudu₃-da mu-ši-ib-ra-an
#lem: namlulu[humanity]; mušen[bird]; ni[fear]; teŋ[approach]; šud[prayer]; rah[beat]
#tr.en: People tremble (?) in prayer before you like frightened birds. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.20

1.21. [...] X zig₃-ga ni₂ ri-a šu# nu#-ra-ab-la₂-e
#lem: X; X; zig[rise]; ni[fear]; ri[impose]; šu[hand]; la[hang]
#tr.en: Rising ……, imbued with awesomeness, no one …… you. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.21

1.22. ni₂# gur₃-ru su zig₃ gur₃-ru ni₂ gal mu-da-ri
#lem: ni[fear]; gur[lift]; su[flesh]; zig[rise]; gur[lift]; ni[fear]; gal[big]; ri[impose]
#tr.en: Of terrifying appearance, endowed with fearsome splendour, you are imbued with great awesomeness. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.22

1.23. [u₄]-ta#-u₁₈-lu lu₂-ra te-a-me-en
#lem: Utaʾulu[1]; lu[person]; teŋ[approach]
#tr.en: You are a hurricane that approaches mankind, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.23

1.24. [...] mah# lu₂-še₃ ur₃-ur₃-ra-me-en
#lem: X; mah[great]; lu[person]; ur[drag]
#tr.en: a great …… that sweeps men down, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.24

1.25. [X X] X lu₂-še₃ bar-bar-ra-me-en
#lem: X; X; X; lu[person]; bar[place outside]
#tr.en: …… that …… mankind! 
#etcsl: line-id=1.25

1.26. [...]-gin₇ kur-ra gana₂ gid₂-gid₂
#lem: X; kur[mountain(s)]; gana[field]; gid[long]
#tr.en: In the mountains you measure the fields like a ……. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.26

1.27. [... an]-ta# šu bar-ra gaba-šu-ŋar nu-tuku
#lem: X; an[sky]; šu[hand]; bar[place outside]; gabašuŋar[rival]; tuku[acquire]
#tr.en: …… emitted from heaven, without compare, ……, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.27

1.28. [...] X ud kur-ra e₃-a
#lem: X; X; ud[sun]; kur[mountain(s)]; e[leave]
#tr.en: who brings daylight to the mountains, ……, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.28

1.29. [...] X ud dug₄-ga du₇-du₇
#lem: X; X; ud[sun]; dug[speak]; du[push]
#tr.en: battering ……, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.29

1.30. [X X] UN MAŠ-a-gin₇ nim ŋir₂-ŋir₂-re
#lem: X; X; X; X; nim[lightning]; ŋir[flash]
#tr.en: ……, who flashes like lightning. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.30

1.31. MI-E₂-A{mušen}-a zi ir lu₂-ra šub-bu
#lem: MI.E₂.A[bird]; zi[life]; ir[cvve]; lu[person]; šub[fall]
#tr.en: Falling upon mankind like a …… bird of grief, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.31

1.32. nam-tar šu nu-tuku ŋiri₃ nu-tuku lu₂ ŋi₆-a tum₂-mu
#lem: Namtar[1]DN; šu[hand]; tuku[acquire]; ŋiri[foot]; tuku[acquire]; lu[person]; ŋi[night]; tum[suitable]
#tr.en: a @fsux{namtar} demon with no hands or feet, suited (?) to the night, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.32

1.33. nam-tar-e-gin₇ ŋi₆-a du-du ZI-LAL₃-gin₇ dim₂-e
#lem: Namtar[1]DN; ŋi[night]; ŋen[go]; X; dim[create]
#tr.en: prowling at night like a @fsux{namtar} demon, ……, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.33

1.34. pu₂-kiri₆ mu₂-sar ŋiš-gi sig₇-ga
#lem: pukiri[irrigated orchard]; musar[garden]; ŋešgi[thicket]; sissig[green-yellow]
#tr.en: shaped like a …… -- you, hero @wDN{Šul-pa-e}, are the lord of orchards and gardens, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.34

1.35. niŋ₂-ur₂-limmu₂ an-edin daŋal-la
#lem: niŋurlimmu[four legged creature]; aneden[the high steppe]; daŋal[wide]
#tr.en: plantations and green reedbeds, of the quadrupeds of the wide high desert, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.35

1.36. maš₂-anše niŋ₂-zi-ŋal₂ edin-na
#lem: mašanše[animals]; niŋziŋal[living creature]; eden[back]
#tr.en: of the animals, the living creatures of the plains. @wDN{An}, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.36

1.37. ur-saŋ {d}šul-pa-e₃ za-e lugal-bi-me-en
#lem: ursaŋ[warrior]; Šulpae[1]DN; zaʾe[you]; lugal[king]
#tr.en: king of the gods, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.37

1.38. an lugal diŋir-re-e-ne-ke₄ šu-za im-ma-an-šum₂
#lem: An[1]DN; lugal[king]; diŋir[deity]; šu[hand]; šum[give]
#tr.en: has put them in your hands; 
#etcsl: line-id=1.38

1.39. [šu-za] im-ma-an-šum₂ za-e lugal-bi-me-en
#lem: šu[hand]; šum[give]; zaʾe[you]; lugal[king]
#tr.en: he has put them in your hands, and you are their lord. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.39

1.40. ur-saŋ {d}šul-pa-e₃-a šu-zu la-ba-ra-e₃
#lem: ursaŋ[warrior]; Šulpae[1]DN; šu[hand]; e[leave]
#tr.en: Hero @wDN{Šul-pa-e}, they cannot escape your clutches. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.40

1.41. u₂ tuku u₂-na ba-ni-in-gu₇!
#lem: u[plant(s)]; tuku[acquire]; u[plant(s)]; gu[eat]
#tr.en: It is his food that anyone who has food eats; it is his water that anyone who has water drinks. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.41

1.42. a tuku a-na ba-ni-in-naŋ
#lem: a[water]; tuku[acquire]; a[water]; naŋ[drink]
#tr.en: And so people no longer call upon the name of their personal gods, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.42

1.43. mu diŋir-ra-na li-bi-in-pad₃-[de₃]
#lem: mu[name]; diŋir[deity]; pad[find]
#tr.en: but …… in every mouth the name of him who is their only god. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.43

1.44. mu diŋir-ra-ni dili-a-bi ka-ga₁₄ mi-ni-X
#lem: mu[name]; diŋir[deity]; dili[single]; kag[mouth]; X
#tr.en: The hand …… of his god ……. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.44

